+        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
+        <p>Last updated November 3, 2026. ShopCrank is operated by Alderman Enterprises LLC DBA ShopCrank ("ShopCrank", "we", "us"). This policy explains what we collect when a subscribing shop and its staff use ShopCrank, what happens to the records a shop keeps about its own customers, and the choices you have.</p>
+
+        <h2>Two kinds of data</h2>
+        <p><strong>Account data</strong> is about the people who use ShopCrank: the shop owner and staff. We decide how it is used, as described here.</p>
+        <p><strong>Shop records</strong> are what a shop enters or receives in ShopCrank about its own customers: names, phone numbers, email and street addresses, vehicles, repair orders, estimates, invoices, payments, inspections, photos, messages and call summaries. The shop controls these records. We process them on the shop's behalf to run the service, and a customer of a shop should contact that shop first about them.</p>
+
+        <h2>What we collect</h2>
+        <ul>
+          <li><strong>Account details:</strong> name, work email, role, shop name, and the sign-in method (a one-time email link or Google). ShopCrank does not store shop passwords; the offline desktop edition keeps a scrambled password check on that computer only.</li>
+          <li><strong>Shop records:</strong> everything a shop types in, imports, uploads or receives through texting, the AI phone assistant and connected services.</li>
+          <li><strong>Payments:</strong> card details are entered on Stripe's hosted pages and never reach ShopCrank. We keep payment amounts, dates and references.</li>
+          <li><strong>Calls and texts:</strong> when the AI phone assistant answers a call, the call is transcribed so the assistant can respond, and a summary with the caller's number is saved for the shop. Audio is not recorded. Text messages sent and received through ShopCrank are stored with their delivery status.</li>
+          <li><strong>Usage and device data:</strong> pages and features used, errors, browser and device type, IP address, and timestamps, used to keep the service working and improve it. Analytics events are tied to your account.</li>
+          <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> one sign-in cookie that keeps you signed in, plus a short-lived cookie during Google sign-in. We do not use advertising cookies.</li>
